              {
                "id": "ps-tips-copy",
                "type": "rich_text",
                "html": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>Annabel's Snacking Tips!</strong></p><p style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>1. Think mini meals, not snacks</strong><br>Treat snacks like fuel – balance carbs, protein, and fruit &amp; veg to keep little tummies fuller for longer.</p><p><strong>2. Keep it colourful</strong><br>A rainbow plate = more nutrients and more chance they’ll actually eat it.</p><p><strong>3. Portion for small hands</strong><br>Finger-friendly sizes help toddlers self-feed.</p><p><strong>4. Routine is everything</strong><br>Offer snacks at set times to avoid constant grazing and protect appetites for meals.</p><p><strong>5. Pair new with familiar</strong><br>Pair “safe” foods + one new food = less pressure, more curiosity.</p>"
